    "title": "Wembanyama Shines in Spurs' Victory Over Mavericks",
    "text": "• Victor Wembanyama scored 40 points and grabbed 15 rebounds.\n• San Antonio Spurs defeated the Dallas Mavericks 125-92.\n• Cooper Flagg, the No. 1 overall pick, made his NBA debut.\n• Flagg scored 10 points and had 10 rebounds in his debut.\n• Dylan Harper scored 15 points for the Spurs off the bench.\n• Stephon Castle, the reigning Rookie of the Year, scored 22 points.\n• Anthony Davis scored 22 points and had 13 rebounds for the Mavericks.\n• Kyrie Irving is recovering from ACL surgery and is likely months away from returning.\n• Wembanyama added three blocks to his performance.\n• Wembanyama was playing in his first regular season game since surgery for deep vein thrombosis.\n• Wembanyama led a 13-0 run late in the first half.\n• The Spurs will play at New Orleans on Friday night.\n• The Mavericks will face Washington on Friday as part of a five-game homestand.",
